1. Builds
---------

  KSU    KernelSU 32704, backslashxx/KernelSU official-compatible driver
  NoSU   no root (use this with Magisk, or without root)

  Latest:        v1 (2026-11-04)
  Version text:  5.10.245-akedore-umrsrn-v1-KSU / -NonKSU
  Zip names:     akedore-kernel-4.19-v1-KSU-UMUM-<date>-beryllium.zip
                 akedore-kernel-4.19-v1-NoSU-UMUM-<date>-beryllium.zip

  The version shows 5.10.245 because Aozora spoofs the version text.
  The real base is Linux 4.19.325.

2. Requirements
---------------

  - POCO F1 (beryllium).
  - A ROM with a 4.19 vendor. It does NOT boot on 4.9 ROMs; for those
    use AKEDORE kernel 4.9. The zip reads the kernel already in boot
    and stops if the ROM is on the other kernel line.
  - A recovery that can flash AnyKernel3 zips (OrangeFox, TWRP).

3. Install
----------

  1. Back up your current boot image in recovery.
  2. Flash the AKEDORE zip in recovery.
  3. Reboot to system.

  To go back: restore the boot backup, or dirty flash the ROM.

4. Root (KSU build)
-------------------

  - Manager: the official KernelSU manager with version 32704
    (KernelSU v3.3.1-24-g528bafc5). Other managers (KernelSU-Next,
    SukiSU, older builds) do not match this driver.
  - Install only ONE KernelSU manager. Uninstall old ones first.
  - KernelSU has no popup: allow root for an app in the manager, then
    force stop and reopen that app.
  - App Profile "Default" gives full root. Templates with limited
    capabilities give limited root.
  - KernelSU has no built-in Zygisk. Use a Zygisk module if you
    need it (for example ReZygisk or NeoZygisk).

5. 4.19 bug fixes
-----------------

  These are known bugs of 4.19 kernels on this phone. Test status is
  given for each one.

  - High standby drain: the SoC never reached system sleep (the
    system-pm driver never bound). Fixed in TEST2.3. Measured: about
    45 mA screen off with Wi-Fi on (before: 55-58 mA).
  - Xiaomi thermal profile never applied on non-MIUI ROMs, and the
    charging temperature limit did nothing. Fixed in TEST2.2.
    Measured: +55 % sustained CPU, xo_therm held near 51 C.
  - Phone powers off on reboot: warm reboot. Tested 10-15 reboots.
  - USB not detected after replugging: fixed. Tested 10-15 replugs,
    USB and MTP show up right away.
  - No "file transfer" menu on PC ports that use USB Power Delivery:
    the port is now reported as USB. Tested on device.
  - Battery drops or shuts off with charge left: fuel-gauge fix
    included, not fully tested yet.
  - Battery cycle count not fully cleared: fixed.

6. Other fixes
--------------

  - Chrome/Brave crash on Android 17: CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE backport.
  - Android 17 bootloop on some ROMs (bpfloader): BPF bind return
    values 0..3 allowed (upstream backport).
  - Bootloop with newer clang: removed an LTO flag from the Aozora
    Makefile that crashed the kernel at boot.
  - Vibrations of 1 s or longer did nothing: haptics timer typo
    (present in every beryllium kernel).
  - QC2 charging thermal typo: 10.2 A corrected to 1.025 A.
  - PD/PPS chargers dropping to 25 mA: charging parameters clamped.
  - Camera: no_i2c switch for phones with a dead autofocus motor
    (off by default).
  - Backports: MGLRU and zram fixes, UFS pm_qos, rmnet/IPA fixes,
    one cpuidle timer per CPU, BBR as the default TCP congestion.

7. Tuner and game boost
-----------------------

  Settings live in /sys/module/fsociety/parameters/ (root):

    profile         0 eco, 1 balanced (default), 2 game
    gpu_autoboost   1 (default) = game boost on, 0 = off
    gpu_boost_busy  GPU busy % that starts the boost (default 85)
    screen_off_cap  1 (default) = lower CPU limits with screen off
    mglru_lock      1 (default) = keep MGLRU on

  - eco:       GPU up to 596 MHz, CPU 1.52 / 2.00 GHz (screen on).
  - balanced:  GPU up to 710 MHz (stock). While a game keeps the GPU
               busy at 710 MHz, it is lifted to 802 MHz; it drops back
               when the load goes down or the screen turns off.
  - game:      GPU up to 802 MHz all the time.
  - screen off: CPU 1.23 / 1.46 GHz for background work.

  These are upper limits only. Thermal (kernel zones, LMH and the
  ROM's thermal-engine) still works on top of them.

  The fsociety Kernel Control module (KernelSU/Magisk, WebUI) switches
  Standard / Gaming and watches battery temperature (47 C, 45 C while
  charging). It is shared with the release zips, not in this repo.

8. Known issues
---------------

  - Double-tap-to-wake is reliable only with Always-On Display on. On
    a replaced (non-original) LCD the touch IC can drop off when the
    screen is fully off, so a tap is not always read.
  - The first USB plug after a cold boot can rarely be missed;
    replugging works.
  - The internal names still say fsociety (/sys/module/fsociety,
    CONFIG_FSOCIETY_TUNER, the control module). This is on purpose, so
    scripts and modules keep working.

9. Reporting a bug
------------------

  Please open a GitHub issue with:

  - ROM name and version, KSU or NoSU build, root solution.
  - What you did and what happened.
  - Logs (root shell):
      dmesg > /sdcard/dmesg.txt
      logcat -b all -d > /sdcard/logcat.txt
    If the phone rebooted or turned off by itself, also:
      cat /sys/fs/pstore/* > /sdcard/pstore.txt

10. Building from source
------------------------

  - Clang/LLVM toolchain (tested: Neutron clang 24) and the
    aarch64-linux-gnu- / arm-linux-gnueabi- binutils.
  - The KSU build needs the KernelSU submodule:
      git submodule update --init
  - Build:
      CLANG_DIR=/path/to/clang ./build_akedore.sh ksu
      CLANG_DIR=/path/to/clang ./build_akedore.sh nosu
  - Output: out/ (ksu) or out-nosu/ (nosu),
    arch/arm64/boot/Image.gz-dtb. Pack it with AnyKernel3.
  - PROFILE=oc builds the old OC device tree (14 thermal zones off).
    It is not used for the release zips.

